{"seq":1,"mint":"C9","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"because in `look_path` the returned bytes and the captured `output` are the same value `shown`","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F9","F16","F28","F32"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"    let mut printed = String::new();\n    printed.push_str(&format!(\"==> {path} <==\\n\"));\n    printed.push_str(&shown);\n    if !shown.is_empty() && !shown.ends_with('\\n') {\n        printed.push('\\n');\n    }\n\n    let entry = PendingEntry {\n        kind: ObservationKind::Path,\n        key,\n        label,\n        output: shown,\n        world_root: world.root,\n        world_state: world.state,\n        captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n        pattern: String::new(),\n    };\n    let mut buf = pending::load(workspace_dir)?;\n    buf.push(entry);\n    pending::save(workspace_dir, &buf)?;\n\n    Ok(LookOutcome { printed })","why":"The captured output is `shown`, but the returned `LookOutcome` contains `printed`, which also includes the header and possibly an added newline.","quoted":true},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"`look_grep` is bounded and `look_path` is not","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F2","F22","F27","F31"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"        for line in stdout.lines() {\n            if let Some((file, rest)) = line.split_once(':') {\n                by_file.entry(file.to_string()).or_default().push(rest.to_string());\n            }\n        }\n        // One whole-search record beside the per-file hits. Without it a\n        // search that matched says only which files it hit, and where it\n        // was rooted — the thing a census turns on — is unrecoverable.\n        // Its marker comes from the search root, exactly as the\n        // zero-match record's always has.\n        let m = world.for_path(root_path);\n        let files = by_file.len();\n        buf.push(PendingEntry {\n            captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n            kind: ObservationKind::Search,\n            key: search_key(root_path, &m.root),\n            label: format!(\n                \"search: {root} (grep: {pattern}) — {files} file{} matched — {note}\",\n                if files == 1 { \"\" } else { \"s\" }\n            ),\n            output: String::new(),\n            world_root: m.root,\n            world_state: m.state,\n            pattern: pattern.to_string(),\n        });\n        for (file, matches) in by_file {\n            let m = world.for_path(Path::new(&file));\n            buf.push(PendingEntry {\n                captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n                kind: ObservationKind::GrepMatch,\n                key: resolve_key(Path::new(&file)),\n                label: format!(\"{file} (grep: {pattern})\"),\n                output: matches.join(\"\\n\"),\n                world_root: m.root,\n                world_state: m.state,\n                pattern: pattern.to_string(),\n            });\n        }","why":"`look_grep` accumulates every line from `stdout` and stores all accumulated matches with no byte-limiting operation, so the captured implementation does not establish a bounded return.","quoted":true}],"at":1790112146,"cost":0.019318259999999997,"elapsed_ms":123784,"attempts":4,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":0}
